Alice68 licensing
=================

Alice68 is distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 only
(GPL-2.0-only). The full text is in COPYING. Individual files keep the licence
their header names; where a file says otherwise, the file wins.

Alice68 is built from the work of others, and it does not relicense any of it.
What is whose is set out in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. In short:

  Emu68 (third_party/Emu68)            MPL-2.0, Michal Schulz and contributors.
                                       Emu68's own files keep their MPL-2.0
                                       notices; changes made to them (by
                                       AGA-PiStorm, FRF or Alice68) are MPL-2.0
                                       too, like the files they change.
  AGA-PiStorm (core/, arm/, tools/,    GPL-2.0-only, Astair86 and contributors.
  package/)                            Its chipset core contains code from UAE
                                       and WinUAE (GPL); package/UAE-WinUAE-
                                       notice.txt collects their copyright lines.
  EMU68AGA Bare Metal (FRF)            GPL-2.0-or-later for FRF-original
                                       material, Future Retro Fusion; FRF's
                                       changes to Emu68's files are MPL-2.0.
  Alice68's additions                  GPL-2.0-only unless the file says
                                       otherwise (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
  Bundled libraries                    their own licences, kept with them:
                                       TinyUSB (MIT), Capstone (BSD-3-Clause and
                                       LLVM), libdeflate (MIT), tiny-stl, libxsvf
                                       (ISC), musl / FreeBSD msun maths (MIT /
                                       Sun), AROS files (AROS Public License).

Why the kernel as a whole is GPL-2.0-only: the AGA chipset core is
GPL-2.0-only (UAE/WinUAE heritage). The kernel combines it with Emu68, which
MPL-2.0 section 3.3 allows; the combined kernel8.img is distributed under the
GPL-2.0, and Emu68's files keep their MPL-2.0 notices (this is how
AGA-PiStorm already distributes its kernels; see its LICENSE in
docs/AGA-PISTORM-LICENSE.txt).

Not part of Alice68 and never distributed with it: Kickstart ROMs and any
other Amiga operating-system files, the Raspberry Pi firmware (start4.elf,
fixup4.dat - get them from the Raspberry Pi firmware repository), the Neptune
USB stack and its classes (rondoval/neptune-usb-stack, AROS Public License),
and games or other commercial software.

"Amiga" is a trademark of its owner. Alice68 is not affiliated with or
endorsed by the owners of that trademark, nor by the Emu68, AGA-PiStorm,
EMU68AGA Bare Metal, PiStorm or Neptune projects. Please report Alice68
problems to Alice68, not to them.
